  "id": "1f3ca337-91d2-528f-891f-85faa614aad0",
  "slug": "slow-cooker-million-dollar-pasta-recipe-11884095",
  "name": "Slow Cooker Million Dollar Pasta",
  "recipe_type": "main",
  "brief_description": "This slow cooker million dollar pasta is rich, cozy, and unapologetically indulgent. Savory beef and tomato sauce soak into the noodles, while the creamy cheese layer melts into a velvety, slightly tangy finish. Every bite tastes like baked ziti crossed with lasagna, but softer, saucier, and deeply comforting.",
  "cuisine": "American",
  "instructions": [
    {
      "position": 1,
      "text": "Heat a large skillet over medium-high heat and add ground beef; cook, stirring occasionally, until well browned, about 6 minutes. Stir in Italian seasoning, pepper, onion powder, and 3 teaspoons of the salt until well combined. Remove from heat."
    },
    {
      "position": 2,
      "text": "Add beef mixture, spaghetti sauce, pasta, and water to a 6-quart slow cooker. Stir until well combined and pasta is fully covered in liquid. Cover and cook on Low until most of the pasta is al dente, about 1 hour and 30 minutes."
    },
    {
      "position": 3,
      "text": "Meanwhile, stir together cream cheese, ricotta, sour cream, Parmesan, parsley, garlic powder, and remaining 3/4 teaspoon salt in a medium bowl until mixture is smooth."
    },
    {
      "position": 4,
      "text": "Dollop and spread cheese mixture evenly over pasta mixture. Sprinkle evenly with mozzarella cheese."
    },
    {
      "position": 5,
      "text": "Cover and continue to cook on Low until pasta is tender and cheese is melted, about 25 minutes more."
    },
    {
      "position": 6,
      "text": "Garnish with parsley and crushed red pepper, if desired. Recipe developed by Amanda Stanfield"
    }
  ],
  "servings": 8,
  "cooking_time_minutes": 115,
